# Every pull request needs a review from the repo owner. This is enforced by
# the `main` ruleset (one approval, code-owner review required); the file is
# what tells GitHub who that owner is, and without it the ruleset's code-owner
# clause has nobody to ask.
#
# Deliberate while the project is young and the contributor list is one person
# plus agents: every change gets a human pass from @Shman4ik before it lands.
# The repository-admin role is a bypass actor on the same ruleset, so the owner
# is not locked out of merging their own work — nobody can approve their own
# pull request, and a solo maintainer with no bypass would be unable to merge
# anything at all.
